{"report": "The 10-year breakeven has drifted higher over longer horizons (+0.16 pp over 252d) but remains anchored tightly to the 2% target, trading only 12 basis points below it. The recent move is one of re-anchoring, not de-anchoring: the breakeven is *closing the gap* to the objective, not widening from it. Over the last 21 days the move is marginal at +4 bp, and the most recent observation (1.88%) sits squarely in the middle of recent history. The 12-month range shows 52 bp of current positioning from its low point, suggesting the market has recovered modestly from lows but has not tested the upper boundary (2.08%).

