The policy language provides no new accommodation of above-target expectations. The FOMC statement repeats "inflation near the Committee's symmetric 2 percent objective" and "a sustained return to 2 percent inflation" with no hedging. Longer-term inflation expectations are characterized as "little changed, on balance," which is consistent with a 2% anchored system experiencing noise around the anchor. The stance remains "accommodative," but that is supporting the existing inflation-targeting framework, not signaling acceptance of permanently higher expectations.

