{"report": "The previous call for higher expectations (conviction 0.62) was correct on direction: the 10-year breakeven has drifted from 1.94% to 1.99%, a +5 bp move in the span since that release. Over 21 days the move is +18 bp, over 63 days +35 bp, over a year +24 bp. The breakeven remains anchored well below the 2% target (now at –1 bp distance), so this is drift within the gravity well, not de-anchoring. The range position at 1.00 (breakeven at the 12-month high of 1.99%) signals the recent momentum has carried it to an upper bound, but not to a pathological extreme.

