{"report": "At the prior release, I called inflation expectations down with 0.25 conviction—a hesitant lean on weak evidence. That call was wrong. Breakeven_10y has moved up +0.10pp over 21 days and +0.11pp over 63 days, now at 2.43%, rallying decisively past my stated falsifier of 2.35%. The current reading sits 0.43pp above the 2% target, still elevated, but the momentum is unmistakably upward. Within the 12-month range (2.12% to 3.02%), the breakeven is now positioned 0.34 on a 0-1 scale, closer to the upper bound than to the lower one. The range_width at 0.90pp is wide—reflecting substantial market uncertainty about the path ahead—but the recent drift is not noise.

